course: dictionary
lesson: 14677
title: Preservation: keeping things safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Preservation is a noun. It comes from the verb preserve, which means to keep something safe and whole. «The park rangers work on the preservation of wildlife in the forest.» The clues are rangers, wildlife and forest, so preservation means protecting nature from harm.
explain: The same word works in the kitchen. «Grandma spent every autumn on food preservation: she salted fish and dried apples so we could eat them all winter.» The clues salted, dried and all winter show that preservation means keeping food fresh for a long time.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The park rangers work on the keeping safe of wildlife» sounds clumsy, but «keeping food fresh» fits the cooking sentence well. Always test your idea before you trust it.
fact: Preservation means keeping something safe from harm, damage or decay.
fact: Preservation also means keeping food fresh for a long time, by drying, salting, freezing or canning.
fact: «In a good state of preservation» means still in good condition, with no damage.
fact: «Self-preservation» means the instinct to keep yourself alive and safe from danger.
fact: Preservation is an uncountable noun, so we say «food preservation» or «the preservation of wildlife», not «a preservation».
exercise: «The museum works hard on the preservation of old paintings.» What does preservation mean here? | *Keeping them safe from damage | Moving them to a new town | Selling them quickly to make money | Painting brand new pictures
exercise: Mum says, «Salting and drying fish is a good way of food preservation.» What is food preservation? | *Keeping food fresh for a long time | Throwing food away | Cooking food very quickly | Buying food from a shop
exercise: «The old coin was still in a good state of preservation.» What does this suggest? | *The coin was still in good condition | The coin was very cheap | The coin was made of wood | The coin was broken into pieces
test: «The reserve works on the preservation of the wetland homes of frogs and birds.» What does preservation of the homes mean? | *Keeping them safe from harm | Counting how many there are | Painting them bright colours | Knocking them down to build roads
test: Which is an example of self-preservation? | *Running away from a dangerous dog to keep yourself safe | Singing in the school choir | Sharing your lunch with a friend | Drawing a picture of a tree
exam: Which way of food preservation keeps food fresh by making it very cold? | Stretching | Singing | *Freezing | Reading
